// EXPECT: FAIL
// ERROR_CONTAINS: ANUBIS_POC_PACK_TYPE
// RUNTIME: exercise via `anubis run` (this is a runtime panic; `anubis check` still passes,
// this is a *runtime* fail-closed gate).
// SILENT_WRONG closed: `anubis_p8` (compiler/src/backends/run.rs POC_KIT_RUNTIME_RS) called
// `v.as_i64() as u8` on any argument. `AnubisValue::List.as_i64()` returns the LIST LENGTH, so
// `p8([9,9,9])` silently produced `[3]` — a byte that means "the list had three elements"
// rather than any element of the list. Payload writers who accidentally pass a list get bytes
// nobody assembled, and the proof-carrying language emits a proof about the wrong artifact.
fn main() {
    print(p8([9, 9, 9]));
}
